    "summary": "Fixed the wchunk package to match the actual binary format found in the sample files. Key changes:\n\n1. **Header format** (header.py): Changed record_count from big-endian u32 at bytes 5-8 to a single u8 at byte 5, with 6 reserved zero bytes (bytes 6-11). Total header remains 12 bytes.\n\n2. **Record format** (codec.py): Replaced LEB128 varint encoding with fixed-width u16LE tag + u16LE size + payload, with each record padded to an 8-byte boundary (zero-filled).\n\n3. **Footer format** (codec.py): Changed from 4-byte footer to 6-byte footer: 4-byte standard CRC-32 (LE u32) covering header + all record bytes (including padding), followed by 2-byte u16LE sum of all record tags.\n\n4. **CRC computation** (crc.py): Fixed compute_crc to use standard zlib.crc32 (removed the erroneous XOR with 0xFFFFFFFF that made it non-standard).\n\n5. **Streaming** (stream.py): Updated iter_records to read fixed-width record headers, handle 8-byte alignment padding, accumulate CRC incrementally over all bytes (head",
    "changed_workspace": true
  },
